---
/**
 * Privacy policy. Draft: the standard structure is filled in with the app's own
 * privacy text, but the owner has not had it reviewed and the registered address
 * and jurisdiction are still open questions (landing/STATUS.md).
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import DocLayout from '../components/DocLayout.astro'
import { BRAND, CONTACT_EMAIL, HAS_CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config/site'
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/ld'
---

<Base path="/privacy" extraLd={[breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' }])]}>
  <DocLayout path="/privacy" title="Privacy policy" lead="How OR² handles information, and the controls you keep over your records." meta={`Effective date to be confirmed · ${BRAND.legalName}`}>
    <div class="notice" slot="notice">
      <p>
        <strong>Draft — needs owner and legal review before it is relied on.</strong> The
        structure and the substance come from {BRAND.name}'s own privacy text. The registered
        entity, its address, the contact route for data requests and the supervisory authority
        are still to be confirmed by {BRAND.legalName}.
      </p>
    </div>


    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {BRAND.legalName} operates {BRAND.name}, a business-operations platform provided to
      registered businesses on an invite-only basis. Businesses use {BRAND.name} to manage stock,
      purchases, sales, accounts and cash flow within their own isolated workspace. The registered
      entity name, registered address and jurisdiction are set out in the schedule at the end of
      this policy, which is to be completed by {BRAND.legalName} before this policy takes effect.
    </p>
    <p>This policy explains how information is handled across the service.</p>

    <h2>The information in {BRAND.name}</h2>
    <p>Information in the service falls into two kinds:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> Details your workspace administrator provides when
        provisioning your account, such as your name, email address, role, and your business's
        details.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Business records.</strong> The records you and your team create in the course of
        running your business: products, bills, payments, ledgers and reports.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <p>The service carries no advertising machinery and no analytics machinery.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No advertising trackers.</li>
      <li>No third-party analytics.</li>
      <li>No profiling of you or your business.</li>
      <li>Nothing is collected beyond what the service needs to run.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This website carries no analytics script, no advertising script and no third-party embed. The
      fonts it uses are served from this site's own origin.
    </p>

    <h2>Your workspace is yours alone</h2>
    <p>
      Every business on {BRAND.name} gets an isolated workspace. Your records are never visible
      to, or shared with, another business.
    </p>
    <p>
      Even {BRAND.legalName} platform staff have no routine view of your business records. Access
      is restricted to the narrow operational needs of running the service.
    </p>

    <h2>How data is protected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Data is encrypted in transit.</li>
      <li>Access to systems is controlled and limited.</li>
      <li>Administration follows least-privilege principles.</li>
      <li>Workspaces are isolated from one another by design.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      You stay in control of your business records. You can export, correct or delete your data at
      any time.
    </p>
    <p>
      When data is deleted, it is removed with no history and no footprints. Deletion in
      {BRAND.name} is complete. The retention period for a workspace that is ended is to be
      confirmed by {BRAND.legalName}.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell, rent or share business data.</p>
    <p>
      The service's infrastructure is hosted by our service providers, who process it under
      obligations that protect it and only on our instructions. Those providers, the categories of
      data they process and the locations they process it in are to be listed by {BRAND.legalName}
      before this policy takes effect.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can exercise the following rights over your account and business records:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access: see the information held in your workspace.</li>
      <li>Correction: fix records that are wrong.</li>
      <li>Export: take your records out of the service.</li>
      <li>Deletion: have records removed with no history and no footprints.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These rights are exercised through your workspace administrator.
      {
        HAS_CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
          <span>
            {' '}
            You can also write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
          </span>
        ) : (
          <span>
            {' '}
            A public address for data requests has not been published yet; it appears here once{' '}
            {BRAND.legalName} confirms it.
          </span>
        )
      }
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will communicate them in advance through the
      service. The effective date at the top of this page reflects the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy are handled through your workspace administrator.</p>

    <h2>Schedule to be completed by {BRAND.legalName}</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Registered entity name, registered address and jurisdiction.</li>
      <li>Public email address for data requests.</li>
      <li>List of infrastructure providers and the data they process.</li>
      <li>Retention period for an ended workspace.</li>
      <li>Effective date.</li>
    </ul>

  </DocLayout>
</Base>
